<article class="env-lemma" id="0EZB">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0EZB">Lemma <span data-tag="0EZB">21.30.4</span>.</a> In Situation <a href="/tag/0EZ3" data-tag="0EZ3">21.30.1</a> if $(V_ n)$ holds, then for $X$ in $\mathcal{C}$ and $L \in D(\mathcal{C}_{\tau '}/X)$ with $H^ i(L) = 0$ for $i < 0$ and $H^ i(L)$ in $\mathcal{A}'_ X$ for $0 \leq i \leq n$ we have $H^ n_{\tau '}(X, L) = H^ n_\tau (X, \epsilon _ X^{-1}L)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      By Lemma <a href="/tag/0D6H" data-tag="0D6H">21.20.5</a> we have $H^ n_\tau (X, \epsilon _ X^{-1}L) = H^ n_{\tau '}(X, R\epsilon _{X, *}\epsilon _ X^{-1}L)$. There is a spectral sequence 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  E_2^{p, q} = R^ p\epsilon _{X, *}\epsilon _ X^{-1}H^ q(L)  \]
</div>
    <p>
       converging to $H^{p + q}(R\epsilon _{X, *}\epsilon _ X^{-1}L)$. By $(V_ n)$ we have the vanishing of $E_2^{p, q}$ for $0 < p \leq n$ and $0 \leq q \leq n$. Thus $E_2^{0, q} = \epsilon _{X, *}\epsilon _ X^{-1}H^ q(L) = H^ q(L)$ are the only nonzero terms $E_2^{p, q}$ with $p + q \leq n$. It follows that the map 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  L \longrightarrow R\epsilon _{X, *}\epsilon _ X^{-1}L  \]
</div>
    <p>
       is an isomorphism in degrees $\leq n$ (small detail omitted). Hence we find that $H^ i_{\tau '}(X, L) = H^ i_{\tau '}(X, R\epsilon _{X, *}\epsilon _ X^{-1}L)$ for $i \leq n$. Thus the lemma is proved. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>